        <mxCell id="notePrice" value="Priced twice, from the database both times

Prices are never taken from the request, so a tampered basket changes nothing — and the customer is charged exactly what the quote showed them." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#78350f;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1410" y="240" width="320" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="noteTx" value="One transaction

Stock, the order, its items and its parcels are written together or not at all. A failure half way cannot leave stock deducted for an order that does not exist." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#78350f;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1410" y="400" width="320" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="noteSplit" value="This is what makes it multi-vendor

Three shops in one basket become three parcels — each collected from a different place, priced on its own distance, and delivered separately.

One delivery fee and one status would have been a fiction." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#eef2ff;strokeColor=#4f46e5;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#4338ca;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1410" y="560" width="320" height="160" as="geometry" />
